## Function Optimizations

### 5. Use External Instead of Public
```solidity
// External is cheaper when called externally
// Public copies calldata to memory
function external process(bytes calldata data) external {}
```

### 6. Use Calldata for Read-Only Arrays
```solidity
// EXPENSIVE
function bad(uint256[] memory data) external {}

// OPTIMIZED
function good(uint256[] calldata data) external {}
```

### 7. Short-Circuit Conditions
```solidity
// Put cheaper checks first
require(cheapCheck() && expensiveCheck());
```

### 8. Use Custom Errors (Solidity 0.8.4+)
```solidity
// EXPENSIVE - stores string
require(balance >= amount, "Insufficient balance");

// OPTIMIZED - 4 bytes
error InsufficientBalance();
if (balance < amount) revert InsufficientBalance();
```

---

## Loop Optimizations

### 9. Unchecked Increment
```solidity
// Standard
for (uint i = 0; i < length; i++) {}

// OPTIMIZED (when overflow impossible)
for (uint i = 0; i < length;) {
    unchecked { ++i; }
}
```

### 10. ++i vs i++
```solidity
// i++ returns old value (costs more)
// ++i returns new value (cheaper)
for (uint i = 0; i < length; ++i) {}
```

### 11. Avoid Redundant Checks in Loops
```solidity
// Move invariants outside loop
uint256 maxAmount = maxPerUser;  // Cache once
for (uint i = 0; i < users.length; ++i) {
    require(amounts[i] <= maxAmount);
}
```

---

## Data Type Optimizations

### 12. Use bytes32 Instead of string
```solidity
// EXPENSIVE
string public name = "Token";

// OPTIMIZED (if <= 32 chars)
bytes32 public constant NAME = "Token";
```

### 13. Use uint256 Over Smaller Types
```solidity
// Counterintuitive: smaller types can cost MORE
// EVM operates on 256-bit words
uint8 a;  // Requires masking operations
uint256 b;  // Native size
```

### 14. Boolean Packing
```solidity
// Use uint256 as bitmap for multiple bools
uint256 flags;  // Can store 256 booleans
function getFlag(uint8 index) view returns (bool) {
    return (flags >> index) & 1 == 1;
}
```

---

## Comparison Optimizations

### 15. != 0 is Cheaper than > 0 for uints
```solidity
// Slightly cheaper
require(balance != 0);
// vs
require(balance > 0);
```

### 16. Use Strict Inequalities
```solidity
// EXPENSIVE
require(a >= b);

// SLIGHTLY CHEAPER (when semantically equivalent)
require(a > b - 1);
```

---

## Event Optimizations

### 17. Index Sparingly
```solidity
// Each indexed param costs extra gas
// Only index what you need to filter by
event Transfer(
    address indexed from,    // Need to filter
    address indexed to,      // Need to filter
    uint256 amount           // Don't need to filter
);
```

---

## Assembly Optimizations (Advanced)

### 18. Direct Storage Access
```solidity
function getSlot(uint256 slot) view returns (uint256 value) {
    assembly {
        value := sload(slot)
    }
}
```

### 19. Efficient Hashing
```solidity
function hash(address a, uint256 b) pure returns (bytes32) {
    assembly {
        mstore(0, a)
        mstore(32, b)
        return(keccak256(0, 64))
    }
}
```

